nk <ST/> <ST/> that one is <ST/> <ST/> fit for any weather <ST/> <ST/> it fits for everything that you want. I do not think that, that is necessarily that question, I think that <ST/> <ST/> we should provide that for them. We <FILL/> <ST/> We have to decide what type of food, because we can't continue <ST/> <ST/> to have multiple things we need to have one and if they choose to bring some from home that's one thing but if <ST/> <ST/> we have to provide that for them <ST/> <ST/> and we need to have that <ST/> <ST/> clarity. Well, I do understand we're going to go under that route, but we have to simplify things, we really have to just make a decision. The directors have asked us to make a decision. <ST/> that is not our <ST/> <ST/> job to decide whether or not we're gonna have this. They said <ST/> <ST/> pick one so we can approve it. So I think we should all decide <ST/> <ST/> on what we need to do and pick something.", "Bert": "<BA/> We just need raw potatoes. My grandfather ate raw potatoes, and he lived till he's ninety five <ST/> It builds character. But <ISSUE/> they don't need any fancy sushi we don't need any fancy burgers <ST/> <ST/> just raw potatoes and maybe some white rice if <UNKNOWN/> <UNKNOWN/> on a good day. <UNKNOWN/> we still continue? OK. Um yeah so that's my opinions on food. I think we should live a more uh <ST/> <ST/> minimalistic lifestyle. And <ST/> OK. <BA/> <BA/> The most important thing is what we don't serve. People have allergies, there's peanut allergies and tree nut allergies and people <ST/> <ST/> are allergic to all kinds of foods, and we don't need any incident here in the office <ST/> <ST/> so we should just have a list of no foods <ST/> <ST/> and then everyone else can bring whatever they want from home. And I think that would just be the best option <ST/> <ST/> for uh everyone's dietary needs <ST/> <ST/> there's no need to be a committee. <UNKNOWN/> <UNKNOWN/> We need <ST/> We need to discuss <UNKNOWN/> setback few <ISSUE/> steps. What is food? Do we eat to live? Do we live to eat? Is it nothing more than an endless cycle of us indulging in the food, and then the food sustaining us so we can continue it? <ST/> these are the kinds of things that we should be discussing. And also, food can also be an activity more than a physical object. The meal itself is <ST/> is <ST/> is a <ST/> is a social bonding situation.", "Walter": "Uh but I think a <FILL/> <ST/> a salad bar would be the best option to have. I <ST/> I mean it's <ST/> it's very healthy, we can have <FILL/> you know quite a variety of different <ST/> <ST/> uh fruits, like eh vegetables to have and protein option such as eggs <ST/> <ST/> tuna <ST/> <ST/> chicken, tofu <ST/> <ST/> <FILL/> and we could have lots of different dressings we could <UNKNOWN/> <ST/> <ST/> we have vinegar and olive oil <ST/> <ST/> uh <UNKNOWN/> <UNKNOWN/> <ST/> Well, the thing is I think that salad's like uh give lots of variety. I mean we think it's just lettuce, tomato, cucumbers, no there's lot's of <UNKNOWN/> <ST/> <ST/> things you could do with the salad. Eh we could have <FILL/> <ST/> uh <ST/> <FILL/> There's Waldorf <FILL/> salad, we could have a <ISSUE/> fruit salad uh we could have you know quinoa and <ST/> <ST/> beets, <UNKNOWN/> , lentils, rice <ST/> <ST/> uh even <ST/> I think we really gotta think about what kind of company do you want. Do we want a company that promotes healthy eating <ST/> <ST/> or do we want a company that just uh provides what they want, I think that <ST/> <ST/> a company that promotes healthy eating <ST/> <ST/> that would give us a very good brand to have. So <ST/> <UNKNOWN/> <ST/> that's something that we have just <ST/> just take into consideration, I mean <ST/> and also giving the proper nutrients is gonna help them perform better. <UNKNOWN/>"}, "duration_s": 362.51, "device": "sc_meetup_0"}
